From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:25:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: let init set the Q25 double-tap to wake

The touch driver's wake_gesture module parameter (kernel patch 0903)
carries the generic sysfs label, so init could not copy Settings'
Double-tap to wake choice into it (sable-dt2w.rc). On the owner's Q25
(2026-11-14) the switch was on, the parameter stayed N, and init logged
avc: denied { write } for name="wake_gesture" scontext=u:r:init:s0
tcontext=u:object_r:sysfs:s0. Label it sysfs_sable_dt2w and let init
write it; no app can.
---
 sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts | 3 +++
 sepolicy/vendor/sable_dt2w.te  | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/vendor/sable_dt2w.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
index 0d3cab9..faae1a4 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
@@ -11,3 +11,6 @@ genfscon proc /firmware_upgrade u:object_r:proc_sable_kbd_fw:s0
 
 # SableOS: trackpad mode switch (bbqX0kbd), 1 arrow keys, 0 pointer; init writes Settings' choice
 genfscon proc /q20_switch_key_mouse u:object_r:proc_sable_trackpad:s0
+
+# SableOS: double-tap to wake switch (synaptics_dsx, kernel 0903); init writes Settings' choice
+genfscon sysfs /module/mtk_touchscreen_hodafonehw/parameters/wake_gesture u:object_r:sysfs_sable_dt2w:s0
diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/sable_dt2w.te b/sepolicy/vendor/sable_dt2w.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bad9369
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/sable_dt2w.te
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# SableOS: /sys/module/mtk_touchscreen_hodafonehw/parameters/wake_gesture, the Q25 touch panel's
+# double-tap to wake (kernel patch 0903). Settings stores the choice in persist.sys.sable.dt2w and
+# init writes the node (system_ext/etc/init/sable-dt2w.rc); no app may write it.
+type sysfs_sable_dt2w, fs_type, sysfs_type;
+
+allow init sysfs_sable_dt2w:file w_file_perms;
-- 
2.43.0

